From 15051423d47fd6075825e20180e89693768d92a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:28:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/46] vulkan: hc_fn split-K partials read contiguous row
 slices; parallel slice sum in pre_mix

The first version cut K into 512-element slices per workgroup for all 24 rows,
which scatters the weight reads into 24 small runs per workgroup (slow on
LPDDR: 16-28 us cold). Workgroup (slice, row) now reduces one contiguous run of
one row (8 slices of 2048 elements, 200 workgroups; the extra row computes the
slice's sum of squares): 5.8 us cold in the server vs 12.1 us for the plain
matvec at n=3. pre_mix stages the partials in shared memory with one load per
invocation before summing them. Test hc_fn weights use realistic magnitudes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
